but the scale of this one in mariposa  county marks an unnerving start to the  wildfire season  on the doorstep of yosemite national  park home to some of the largest and  oldest trees in the world  the fire has ripped through a handful of  rural homes and businesses but threatens  thousands more  and remains out of control  they came by about 15 20 minutes ago and  told us that everybody's got to go about  four o'clock the power went out  and the fire has been coming towards us  faster and faster  a huge evacuation order is in place more  than six thousand people have left their  homes already as the fire traveled at  frightening speed  spitting out embers that fell as far as  two miles away  this wildfire comes as a record heat  wave is sweeping the united states with  heat warnings and emergencies declared  in several states  everything that's burning in the fire is  extremely dry we know that california  has been dry the last few years and has  gotten drier we just ask that the public  be patient if their  neighborhood or their community has been  affected by the fire it will take a  little while to notify them if they have  if their residents have been affected  climate change is driving the ferocity  of these fires the intense heat and  worse drought in decades spanning the  flames  but so far america has found no  political consensus on a way forward  that will do anything to prevent more of  this in the future  sally lockwood sky news washington
 

